 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "like + -ing, want + to, enjoy + -ing",
   "en": "verb patterns: like doing, want to do, enjoy doing"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "enjoy, like, hate, finish, stop 뒤에는 보통 동사의 -ing형이 옵니다. want, plan, hope, decide 뒤에는 to + 동사원형이 옵니다. like와 hate는 -ing와 to 둘 다 쓸 수 있지만 -ing가 더 자연스럽습니다.",
   "en": "After enjoy, like, hate, finish and stop we usually use the -ing form. After want, plan, hope and decide use to + base verb. Like and hate can take either, but -ing is more natural for general likes."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "enjoy + -ing",
     "I enjoy cooking."
    ],
    [
     "want + to",
     "I want to travel."
    ],
    [
     "plan + to",
     "I plan to move next year."
    ],
    [
     "hate + -ing",
     "I hate washing up."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "enjoy / finish / stop + -ing.",
    "en": "enjoy / finish / stop + -ing."
   },
   {
    "ko": "want / plan / hope / decide + to + 동사.",
    "en": "want / plan / hope / decide + to + verb."
   },
   {
    "ko": "enjoy to cook는 틀립니다.",
    "en": "enjoy to cook is wrong."
   }
  ],
